 "verdict": "ATTENUATED WITH TIME-DOMAIN LOADING: the displaced residual attenuates on uniform-Gaia legs (p=0.283 vs 6.45e-07 sub-threshold) while retaining the same positive sign on every channel.  Three mechanism results sharpen the reading: (1) the anomaly's full-strength carrier on sub-threshold legs is the leg-disagreement channel (p=0.000776), and in-cap perihelion-time uncertainty stays elevated after controlling for observation count (p=0.0257) -- the signature is already expressed as a time-domain disagreement, not only a spatial rotation; (2) the seed-lock account fails -- in-cap element displacement from the catalogue seed grows with Gaia fraction (del_pdeg rho=0.31), so the attenuation is not the fit being pinned to an absorbed solution; (3) the attenuation decomposes predominantly into transit epoch rather than reduction system -- the in-cap amplitude declines with perihelion epoch (rho=-0.54, p=1.38e-05), the residual shows no leg-system-asymmetry dependence that stitching requires (rho=0.06, p=0.411), and the composition correlation partialled on epoch drops to rho=-0.22 (p=0.0986): uniform-Gaia legs are the latest-transiting cohort, and the displaced lobe is intrinsically weakest there.  The epoch gradient is itself a registered measurement (the displaced structure was strongest nearest the transition); (4) the in-cap inclination imbalance flagged by T6 does not mediate the carrier -- ddirf is i-robust (in/out sign preserved in every inclination tercile, i-adjusted contrast unchanged) -- and the uniform-Gaia flatness is genuine amplitude loss rather than underpowering: at the stratum's own sample sizes a sub-threshold-strength effect is detected with 98 per cent power.  What remains open is the residual composition term at late epochs, and the NG-parameter channel is underpowered (n_in=4 in-cap members).",
 "evidence_status": "mechanism audit",
 "inputs": [
  "results/step_b92_refit.jsonl (post-2017 dual-leg refit)",
  "results/step_b91_refit.jsonl (pre-2018 refit)",
  "data/raw/mpc/obs/*.json (per-observation astcat labels)",
  "data/raw/mpc/sbdb_fp/*.json (NG model_pars + element sigmas)"
 ],
 "caveats": [
  "Cross-arc RMS couples leg-fit quality to leg disagreement; the in-cap/out-cap contrast isolates the directional term only if fit-quality floors are composition-matched -- T6 provides that match.",
  "NG solutions exist for a minority of comets and are not randomly assigned: a rate contrast tests whether the catalogue *needed* the parameters, not whether the parameters are real forces.",
  "Element sigmas are catalogue self-reports with heterogeneous fitting conventions; sigma ratios within one record are more comparable than sigmas across records."
 ]
}